---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import ApiDemo from '../components/marketing/ApiDemo.astro';
import Closing from '../components/Closing.astro';
import '../styles/marketing.css';
const features=[
 {number:'01',icon:'route',title:'Choose your route.',text:'Use the exact access profile, proxy class and country approved for the destination.',link:'Explore access profiles',href:'/docs/profiles'},
 {number:'02',icon:'file',title:'Inspect the evidence.',text:'Read source status, final URL, content type and response body, then apply your own validation.',link:'Read the fetch reference',href:'/docs/fetch'},
 {number:'03',icon:'lock',title:'Keep the same key.',text:'Persist the request before dispatch. Recover its saved state and follow the returned retry guidance.',link:'Understand recovery',href:'/docs/recovery'},
];
---
<Layout title="Built for developers — FetchX" description="Connect FetchX to your application with native HTTP requests, approved source profiles and durable recovery. Explore cURL, JavaScript and Python examples.">
 <div class="mkt"><div class="mkt-container"><header class="mkt-page-intro mkt-developer-intro"><div><span class="mkt-eyebrow"><Icon name="code" size={16}/> THE API IS THE INTERFACE</span><h1>Your stack.<br/><span class="mkt-muted">The whole web ahead.</span></h1><p>Bring source access into the tools you already use. Native HTTP requests, inspectable responses and a clear path to recovery.</p><div class="mkt-actions"><a class="mkt-button mkt-button-primary" href="/docs">Open the quickstart <Icon name="arrow" size={18}/></a><a class="mkt-button mkt-button-secondary" href="/docs/fetch">Read the API reference <Icon name="arrow" size={17}/></a></div></div><div class="mkt-developer-aside"><span class="mkt-micro">BRING YOUR OWN STACK</span><div><span>cURL</span><span>JavaScript</span><span>Python</span><span>Any HTTP client</span></div><p>No special SDK required.<br/>Start with the protocol you know.</p><code>POST /v2/fetch</code></div></header>
 <section class="mkt-developer-example"><div class="mkt-section-heading"><div><span class="mkt-eyebrow">01 / MAKE THE CONNECTION</span><h2>One request.<br/><span class="mkt-muted">Start here.</span></h2></div><p>Get your provisioned endpoint, project token and approved source profile. Save your request, then make the call.</p></div><ApiDemo id="developer-example"/></section>
 <section class="mkt-section"><div class="mkt-developer-features">{features.map(feature=><article><div class="mkt-problem-top"><Icon name={feature.icon} size={24}/><span>{feature.number}</span></div><h3>{feature.title}</h3><p>{feature.text}</p><a class="mkt-text-link" href={feature.href}>{feature.link}<Icon name="arrow" size={15}/></a></article>)}</div></section>
 <section class="mkt-developer-paths"><div><span class="mkt-eyebrow">02 / TWO DOCUMENTED PATHS</span><h2>HTTP fetches.<br/><span class="mkt-muted">Browser workflows.</span></h2><p>Use the interface that matches your provisioned gateway and approved execution path.</p></div><div class="mkt-path-cards"><a href="/docs/fetch"><span class="mkt-tag">HTTP API</span><code>/v2/fetch</code><h3>A direct path to the response.</h3><p>Approved source profiles, explicit routing, retained content and durable idempotency.</p><span class="mkt-text-link">Fetch API reference <Icon name="arrow" size={15}/></span></a><a href="/docs/workflow-fetch"><span class="mkt-tag">REVIEWED RECIPES</span><code>/v1/fetch</code><h3>For sources that need a browser.</h3><p>Run reviewed browser and collection recipes enabled on your project’s gateway.</p><span class="mkt-text-link">Workflow fetch reference <Icon name="arrow" size={15}/></span></a></div></section>
 <section class="mkt-open-source"><div class="mkt-open-source-icon"><Icon name="code" size={38}/></div><div><span class="mkt-eyebrow">INTEGRATION GUIDES</span><h2>Plan your integration.</h2><p>Explore guides on rendering, proxy routing and reliable web requests.</p></div><a class="mkt-button mkt-button-secondary" href="/resources">Explore the guides <Icon name="arrow" size={17}/></a></section>
 </div><Closing/></div><script>import '../scripts/marketing.ts';</script>
</Layout>
